Subject: [PATCH] panvk: add v9 to the build matrix

STATUS: HISTORICAL / ILLUSTRATIVE - does not apply to the base commit.

Two reasons it will not apply with `git apply` from the repo root:

  1. The ---/+++ paths are bare filenames ("meson.build"), not "a/"-prefixed
     repo-relative paths. The real file is src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build.
  2. It was authored against a different Mesa revision. Its context expects
     `foreach arch : [6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]`, but base commit
     6598829019c0746aa8e473b4ae1c980cbfa6ea4b has
     `foreach arch : [6, 7, 10, 12, 13, 14]` - no arch 11.

Kept because it is the clearest minimal statement of "v9 was excluded from the
build matrix on purpose". **The applicable patch is
0014-panvk-v9-arch-enablement-common.patch**, which makes the same two changes
(jm_archs and the foreach list) against the correct base.

This patch is necessary but nowhere near sufficient - see docs/why-v9-is-a-port.md.

--- meson.build.pre-v9	2026-09-05 10:59:49.024750504 +0000
+++ meson.build	2026-09-05 11:01:57.304750512 +0000
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 fifthgen_inc_dir = ['fifthgen']
 fifthgen_files = []
 
-jm_archs = [6, 7]
+jm_archs = [6, 7, 9]
 jm_inc_dir = ['jm']
 jm_files = [
   'jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c',
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@
   sha1_h,
 ]
 
-foreach arch : [6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]
+foreach arch : [6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]
   per_arch_files = common_per_arch_files
   inc_panvk_per_arch = []
 
